<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cimon</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 510–450 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century-bce">5th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cimon was an Athenian statesman and general, son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/miltiades">Miltiades</a>, who led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delian-league">Delian League</a> in the decades after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greco-persian-wars">Persian Wars</a>. Around 466 BCE he destroyed a Persian fleet and army at the Eurymedon river, and in 463 BCE he reduced rebellious Thasos. A supporter of friendship with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sparta">Sparta</a>, he was ostracised in 461 BCE but later recalled, and he died on campaign in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyprus">Cyprus</a> about 450 BCE.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cimon.jpg" alt="Cimon" width="320" height="481" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Markus Leupold-Löwenthal · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:KimonSculpture.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
